3 Quickstart
************

3.1 Clone the repository
========================

git clone https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain.git
cd jotain

3.2 Enter the development shell
===============================

Jotain ships a devenv (https://devenv.sh) shell that provides the
tooling -- ‘just’, ‘nil’, ‘nixfmt-rfc-style’, ‘treefmt’, Nix linters,
the language servers the config shells out to, and the fonts the UI
config looks up.  Emacs itself is *not* in the shell (see Launching
Emacs (/usage/launching)); it is built via Nix on demand.  With ‘direnv’
installed the shell activates automatically; otherwise enter it
manually:

devenv shell

3.3 Build and run Emacs with the Jotain configuration
=====================================================

just run-built            # build for the current platform, then launch result/bin/emacs
just run-built-debug      # same, with --debug-init and debug-on-error

   ‘just run-built’ builds the full distribution (Emacs 31 + packages +
tree-sitter grammars -- usually a binary-cache pull, not a compile) and
launches ‘./result/bin/emacs’ with ‘--init-directory=<repo>’, so it
never touches ‘~/.emacs.d’.  The first launch bootstraps any package not
provided by Nix from MELPA; subsequent launches load from the package
cache.

   The direct-launch recipes (‘just run’, ‘just debug’, ‘just tty’,
‘just daemon’, ‘just client’, ‘just client-tty’, ‘just quick’) are
currently disabled stubs -- see the note in Launching Emacs
(/usage/launching), which also covers the daemon + client pattern and
the ‘emd’ / ‘em’ / ‘emg’ shell aliases via
‘services.jotain.shellAliases’.

3.4 Sanity-check the configuration
==================================

just check          # nix flake check: package builds, Nix linting, docs checks,
                    # elisp paren check, byte-compile (warnings as errors), ERT tests
just test           # build only the elisp-test flake check (ERT tests under test/)
just fmt            # nix fmt — treefmt with nixfmt-rfc-style, deadnix, statix

3.5 Clean build artifacts
=========================

just clean          # .elc files, autosaves, eln-cache, result/
just clean-all      # also elpa/, var/, .dev-home/ — forces a full re-fetch

3.6 Update pinned sources
=========================

‘flake.lock’ is the single source of truth for input revs; ‘devenv.yaml’
mirrors the shared ones (‘nixpkgs’, ‘treefmt-nix’, ‘emacs-overlay’).

just update             # update every flake input, then sync devenv.yaml + devenv.lock
just verify             # assert flake.lock and devenv.lock agree on every shared input


