Appendix A Module Options
*************************

A.1 Jotain -- Module Options Reference
======================================

Auto-generated reference for all Nix module options exposed by Jotain
(https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain).

   • Home Manager Module -- per-user Emacs daemon, client wrapper,
     desktop entry
   • System Module -- overlay and system packages
   • devenv Module -- Emacs Lisp development environment

   ------------------------------------------------

A.2 Home Manager Module
=======================

Import and enable in your Home Manager configuration:

{
  imports = [ jotain.homeManagerModules.default ];
  services.jotain = {
    enable = true;
    defaultEditor = true;
    client.enable = true;
  };
}

A.2.1 services.jotain.enable
----------------------------

Whether to enable the Jotain Emacs daemon.

   _Type:_ boolean

   _Default:_

false

   _Example:_

true

   _Declared by:_

   • modulenix (https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain/blob/main/module.nix)

A.2.2 services.jotain.package
-----------------------------

Custom Jotain Emacs package to use.  Leave this unset to use the default
distribution from ‘emacs.nix’ (pgtk/Wayland GUI on Linux, patched NS GUI
on Darwin).

   _Type:_ null or package

   _Default:_

null

   _Declared by:_

   • modulenix (https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain/blob/main/module.nix)

A.2.3 services.jotain.authSources
---------------------------------

Extra authinfo/netrc file paths to hand to Emacs's ‘auth-sources’,
searched ahead of ‘~/.authinfo(.gpg)’ and the 1Password backend.  Point
these at runtime secret files a secret manager produces (sops-nix,
agenix, ...) -- the entries are file _paths_, not the secrets
themselves, and are passed to the daemon through the
‘JOTAIN_AUTH_SOURCES’ environment variable that lisp/init-systems.el
reads.  Every package that consults auth-source (gptel, ‘forge’,
smtpmail, circe) then resolves credentials from them; the ‘eca’ server,
which reads only its environment, additionally has its provider keys
exported from auth-source before each session (see ‘lisp/init-ai.el’).

   _Type:_ list of string

   _Default:_

[ ]

   _Example:_

[
  "/run/secrets/authinfo"
]

   _Declared by:_

   • modulenix (https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain/blob/main/module.nix)

A.2.4 services.jotain.claudeCode.enable
---------------------------------------

Whether to enable the Claude Code CLI (‘claude’) on the wrapper PATH,
the external agent ‘claude-code-ide’ (lisp/init-ai.el, ‘C-c q’) drives.
Pulls the unfree ‘claude-code’ package, so it needs ‘allowUnfree’ .

   _Type:_ boolean

   _Default:_

false

   _Example:_

true

   _Declared by:_

   • modulenix (https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain/blob/main/module.nix)

A.2.5 services.jotain.client.enable
-----------------------------------

Whether to enable generation of Jotain client desktop file.

   _Type:_ boolean

   _Default:_

false

   _Example:_

true

   _Declared by:_

   • modulenix (https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain/blob/main/module.nix)

A.2.6 services.jotain.client.arguments
--------------------------------------

Command-line arguments to pass to ‘emacsclient’.

   _Type:_ list of string

   _Default:_

[
  "-c"
]

   _Declared by:_

   • modulenix (https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain/blob/main/module.nix)

A.2.7 services.jotain.defaultEditor
-----------------------------------

Whether to configure ‘emacsclient’ as the default editor using the
‘EDITOR’ and ‘VISUAL’ environment variables.

   _Type:_ boolean

   _Default:_

true

   _Example:_

false

   _Declared by:_

   • modulenix (https://github.com/Jylhis/jotain/blob/main/module.nix)

A.2.8 services.jotain.devenv.enable
-----------------------------------

Whether to enable the ‘devenv’ CLI on the wrapper PATH, for the native
environment loader (‘devenv-env-global-mode’, lisp/devenv.el) under
launchd/systemd daemons whose login shell does not export it.  Opt-in
because exec-path-from-shell normally finds the user's own devenv, and
‘pkgs.devenv’ bundles its own nix and can version-skew against
